  "final_message": "Order responses from the orders service now include a `total` field in major units, so a $12.50 order returns `total: 12.5` and the storefront doesn't have to convert. `npm test` passes (39 tests) and `npm run arch` reports no new violations. I didn't run `npm run typecheck` separately.\n\n- **Where it shows up:** `POST /orders`, `GET /orders/{id}`, `GET /orders` and `POST /orders/{id}/cancel`. They all build the response in `toOrderResponse` in `src/api/responses.ts`.\n- **Existing field:** `totalCents` is unchanged.\n- **Currencies:** the conversion is in a new `toMajorUnits` in `src/core/money.ts`. It uses each currency's own number of decimals, so JPY and KRW come out as whole numbers (1250 JPY gives `1250`).\n- **Events not changed:** I left the `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` events alone. They are versioned, and nothing in the request was about them.\n- **Tests and docs:** I updated the two assertions in `test/app.test.ts` that check the exact response shape. I also added `total` to the response shape in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n\nI didn't add a test for the JPY and KRW case.",
